        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "94b0ab54-b8a4-5285-b2ae-29f8c311083f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Irish National Caucus, Ancient Order of Hibernians, American Irish Political Education Committee\n- People: Father Sean Gabriel Mc Manus, Seán McManus, John Finucanne, Seán MacBride\n- Concepts: MacBride Principles\n\nFacts:\n- The Ancient Order of Hibernians was founded in New York City in 1836, and its largest membership is now in the United States.\n- The Irish National Caucus was founded by Father Sean Gabriel Mc Manus on February 6, 1974, at a meeting of the Ancient Order of Hibernians.\n- The MacBride Principles were launched in November 1984.\n- Seán McManus and the Irish National Caucus promoted the MacBride Principles.\n- John Finucanne and the American Irish Political Education Committee promoted the MacBride Principles.\n- Nobel Laureate Seán MacBride, a founding member of Amnesty International, drafted the MacBride Principles.",
